{"title":"WATER SPILLED FROM SOURCE TO USE","link":"https://ghuneim.com/2025/11/23/water-spilled-from-source-to-use/","date":1763861417000,"content":"<p><a href=\"https://ghuneim.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/34D7AE6E-D86A-4014-996F-03CDC060B6D1_1_201_a.jpeg\"><img src=\"https://ghuneim.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/34D7AE6E-D86A-4014-996F-03CDC060B6D1_1_201_a.jpeg\" alt=\"&quot;WATER SPILLED FROM SOURCE TO USE&quot; is the title of a 1984 conceptual art work by Lawrence Weiner, displayed as text on the facade of a building at 488 Greenwich Street in New York City. The phrase refers to a process where, in transit, some water is inevitably lost or &quot;spilled,&quot; which can have different effects, such as causing rust or making something grow. Weiner describes the work as a &quot;sculpture made of language and other materials,&quot; where the words are the sculpture and the materials are what's being referred to. \nArtist: Lawrence Weiner\nTitle: &quot;WATER SPILLED FROM SOURCE TO USE&quot;\nDate: 1984\nLocation: 488 Greenwich Street, New York City\nMedium: Text/language as sculpture\nMeaning: The phrase, used as a sculpture, highlights the idea that nothing is perfect in transit. Some of the water is lost on the way from its source to its final use, with the potential for both negative (corrosive) and positive (growth) outcomes. \nF.Y.I. - The New York Times\nSep 17, 1994 — The slogan &quot;Water Spilled From Source to Use&quot; appears on a 1984 sculpture by conceptual artist Lawrence Weiner. The sc...\n\nThe New York Times\n\nI wasn't sure what to make of the WATER SPILLED FROM ...\nMar 19, 2024 — Rob Stephenson (@robstephoto) March 20, 2024 at 7:10 AM. ·Author. A little research led me to conceptual artist Lawren...\n\nThreads\nA House That Memorializes a Vanished New York\nSep 3, 2024 — Today, even from the outside, the Federal-style building on Greenwich Street stands in striking contrast to the area's .\" width=\"3715\" height=\"2786\" srcset=\"https://ghuneim.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/34D7AE6E-D86A-4014-996F-03CDC060B6D1_1_201_a.jpeg 3715w, https://ghuneim.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/34D7AE6E-D86A-4014-996F-03CDC060B6D1_1_201_a-768x576.jpeg 768w, https://ghuneim.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/34D7AE6E-D86A-4014-996F-03CDC060B6D1_1_201_a-1536x1152.jpeg 1536w, https://ghuneim.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/34D7AE6E-D86A-4014-996F-03CDC060B6D1_1_201_a-2048x1536.jpeg 2048w, https://ghuneim.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/34D7AE6E-D86A-4014-996F-03CDC060B6D1_1_201_a-960x720.jpeg 960w\" /></a></p>","author":"MDG","siteTitle":"Mark Ghuneim","siteHash":"fbdbfb355dab5247b3a3d9c04401313e99252873a1ae0fb1ea729c2e5736c6f3","entryHash":"b85be82db3976de2a2ec1f8698ebff6486cca3bb22fcef1cd79058ce0ff07520","category":"Sites"}